      "body": "### \ud83d\udd0e Search Terms\n\nrecursive, constraint, satisfies, return type inference, 64311\n\n### \ud83d\udd57 Version & Regression Information\n\n- Introduced by #64311 (`7.1.0-dev.20260918.1`), still present in `7.1.0-dev.20260929.1`. Before #64311 the declaration was a circularity error.\n\n### \u23ef Playground Link\n\n_No response_\n\n### \ud83d\udcbb Code\n\n```ts\ninterface Schema<O> { readonly out: O }\ntype Shape = Record<string, Schema<any>>;\ntype Lookup = { x: 1; dflt: 2 };\ndeclare function object<S extends Shape, P extends keyof Lookup>(shape: S): Schema<{ [K in keyof S]: S[K][\"out\"] }> & { p: P; f: (x: P) => void };\ndeclare const str: Schema<string>;\n\nconst u = object({ name: str }) satisfies { p: number | \"x\" };\nu.f(42); // error, P is \"x\"\n\nconst t = object({ name: str, get rec() { return object({ inner: t }); } }) satisfies { p: number | \"x\" };\nt.f(42); // no error\nconst tp: \"x\" = t.p; // error: Type 'number | \"x\"' is not assignable to type '\"x\"'\n```\n\n### \ud83d\ude41 Actual behavior\n\n`P` on `t` is `number | \"x\"`, outside `keyof Lookup`, with no diagnostic. `P` only has a return-type inference from `satisfies`. The outer resolution filters it by the constraint, the re-entrant one doesn't, and `typeof t` ends up with the re-entrant result. With two mutually recursive consts only the one that resolves first gets the leaked type, so swapping the declaration order moves the error. Wes raised this in review: https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/pull/64311#pullrequestreview-5239678270\n\n### \ud83d\ude42 Expected behavior\n\n`P` is `\"x\"` on `t` as it is on `u`, and `t.f(42)` is an error.\n\n### Additional information about the issue\n\n_No response_\n",
